{{other uses|#Styles}}
[[File:LiquidMolly's home recording studio - overview.jpg|thumb|Indie music is known for its [[Do it yourself|DIY]], low-budget approach to music.]]
'''Independent music''' (also commonly known as '''indie music''', or simply '''indie''') is a broad style of music characterized by creative freedom, low budgets, and a [[Do it yourself|do-it-yourself]] approach to music creation. It originated from the liberties afforded by [[Independent record label|independent record labels]]. Indie music describes a number of related styles, but generally refers to guitar-oriented music that deviates from mainstream conventions. There are a number of [[Music subgenre|subgenres]] of independent music which combine its characteristics with other genres, such as [[indie pop]], [[indie rock]], [[indie folk]], and [[Electronic music#Indie electronic|indie electronic]]. Additionally, in certain circles, the term indie has taken on a definition entirely based on the typical sound of independent music in the 1980s, losing its connection to production style.

The origins of independent music lie in the early distribution of private press albums from the 1960s–1970s<ref>{{Cite web |title=Loners and lovers: uncovering the rich, intimate history of private press records |website=The Vinyl Factory |url=https://www.thevinylfactory.com/features/history-of-private-press-record-releases |access-date=2025-06-28}}</ref> as well as late '70s British independent record labels, from the early alternative music scene such as [[Rough Trade Records|Rough Trade]], [[Factory Records|Factory]], [[Industrial Records]] and [[Mute Records|Mute]], which later contributed to the development of [[alternative rock]] music. ''[[NME]]'' released the influential compilation album ''[[C86]]'' in 1986, which helped define [[indie rock]]. American independent music first emerged in the 1980s, and was spread via [[Campus radio|college radios]], which led to the term [[college rock]]. Styles that evolved out of indie music and reached wide commercial success in the 1990s include [[grunge]] ([[Nirvana (band)|Nirvana]], [[Pearl Jam]]) and [[Britpop]] ([[Blur (band)|Blur]], [[Pulp (band)|Pulp]], and [[Oasis (band)|Oasis]]). In the [[21st century]], due to the internet, indie music saw a global spread in popularity, as music fans were no longer dependent on physical publications to find new music.

Independent record labels, important to the development of indie music, are characterized by their smaller operations, lower funding, and greater creative control as compared to [[Record label|major labels]]. Independent labels use a variety of methods of distribution, with the label generally owning the copyright for the sound recording. They generally give smaller [[Advance against royalties|advances]], or sometimes no advance, and some may offer higher royalty splits than major labels.

{{short description|Planning technique}}
{{more citations needed|date=August 2014}}
A '''technology roadmap''' is a flexible [[plan]]ning schedule to support strategic and long-range planning, by matching short-term and long-term goals with specific [[technology]] solutions.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal|last1=Phaal|first1=Robert|last2=Farrukh|first2=Clare J.P.|last3=Probert|first3=David R.|title=Technology roadmapping—A planning framework for evolution and revolution|journal=Technological Forecasting and Social Change|volume=71|issue=1–2|pages=5–26|doi=10.1016/s0040-1625(03)00072-6|year=2004|s2cid=17365217 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.entrepreneur.com/technology/techtrendscolumnistpeteralexander/article83000.html|title=Creating a Technology Road Map|first=Peter|last=Alexander|date=1 January 2006|website=Entrepreneur |access-date=2 April 2018}}</ref> It is a plan that applies to a new product or process and may include using [[technology forecasting]] or [[technology scouting]] to identify suitable [[emerging technologies]].<ref name=GARCIA97 /> It is a known technique to help manage the [[Fuzzy Front End|fuzzy front-end]] of innovation.<ref>{{Cite journal|last1=Oliveira|first1=Maicon G.|last2=Rozenfeld|first2=Henrique|title=Integrating technology roadmapping and portfolio management at the front-end of new product development|journal=Technological Forecasting and Social Change|volume=77|issue=8|pages=1339–1354|doi=10.1016/j.techfore.2010.07.015|year=2010}}</ref> It is also expected that roadmapping techniques may help companies to survive in turbulent environments<ref name=":0" /> and help them to plan in a more holistic way to include non-financial goals and drive towards a more sustainable development.<ref>{{Cite journal|last1=Petrick|first1=Irene J.|last2=Echols|first2=Ann E.|title=Technology roadmapping in review: A tool for making sustainable new product development decisions|journal=Technological Forecasting and Social Change|volume=71|issue=1–2|pages=81–100|doi=10.1016/s0040-1625(03)00064-7|year=2004}}</ref> Here roadmaps can be combined with other corporate foresight methods to facilitate [[systemic change]].<ref>{{Cite journal|last1=Rohrbeck|first1=René|last2=Kallehave|first2=Pernille|date=2012-06-01|title=The Role of Corporate Foresight in Promoting Sustainability|url=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/256021070|journal=Global Compact International Yearbook|volume=2012}}</ref>

Developing a roadmap serves three primary purposes.<ref name="GARCIA97">Garcia, M.L. and Bray, O.H. (1997). "Fundamentals of Technology Roadmapping". Strategic Business Development Department, Sandia National Laboratories. [http://prod.sandia.gov/techlib/access-control.cgi/1997/970665.pdf]</ref> Firstly, it aids in reaching a consensus on a set of needs and the technologies necessary to address them. Secondly, it offers a mechanism for forecasting technological advancements. Thirdly, it supplies a framework for planning and coordinating technology developments.<ref>{{Cite book|title=Technologie-Roadmap : strategisches und taktisches Technologiemanagement; ein Leitfaden|last=Thorsten.|first=Laube|date=2006|publisher=Fraunhofer-IRB-Verl|others=Abele, Thomas.|isbn=978-3816771869|location=Stuttgart|oclc=180950449}}</ref> Additionally, it can function as an analytical tool for charting the evolution and rise of new industries.

