In the physical sciences, '''relaxation''' usually means the return of a perturbed system into [[thermodynamic equilibrium|equilibrium]].
Each relaxation process can be categorized by a '''relaxation time''' [[tau|&tau;]]. The simplest theoretical description of relaxation as function of time ''t'' is an exponential law {{math|exp(−''t''/''&tau;'')}} ([[exponential decay]]).
